== the help documents the forms and $KOSHCONF:
DESCRIPTION
  Koshka settings and their binary KOSHCONF form can be read and written here.
  The save form can print the current settings for a child kosh. With --persist,
  it also writes them to the user configuration file.

SYNOPSIS
  koshconf create <bash|sh|kosh> [--force]
  koshconf set <option> <value> [--persist]
  koshconf get <option>
  koshconf list [-a|--all]
  koshconf load <base64>
  koshconf save [--persist]

OPTIONS
      --help                            Display help.
  -a, --all                             When list is used, also show the
                                        posix.legacy and bash.legacy spelling of
                                        each option.
      --persist                         When set is used, also write the option
                                        to the user configuration file. When
                                        save is used, write the settings that
                                        differ from the defaults of the current
                                        mood to that file.
      --force                           When create is used, replace an existing
                                        configuration file.
